      en: "The Tchiamba-Nzassi oil field is located offshore Pointe-Noire in the Atlantic Ocean and is one of the most productive offshore fields in the Republic of the Congo. Discovered in 1985 and commissioned in 1990, extraction occurs via multiple platforms in water depths of 50 to 200 meters. Daily production averages 80,000 barrels of crude oil, accounting for about 40% of national output. The operator is a joint venture between the Congolese national oil company SNPC and international partners such as TotalEnergies and Eni. Oil is transported via pipelines to the Pointe-Noire port. The field has an estimated remaining lifespan of 20 years. Revenues from Tchiamba-Nzassi are a critical support for the state budget, funding infrastructure projects.",
