      en: "The Yie substation is a key switching station in the Republic of the Congo's power grid, located about 15 kilometers northeast of Brazzaville. Commissioned in 2012 as part of the Central African Economic Community (CEMAC) energy infrastructure project, it steps down high voltage from 220 kV to 90 kV and 33 kV, supplying much of the capital region and industrial areas. The substation is connected to the Djoué and Moukoukoulou hydroelectric plants. With a transmission capacity of 800 MVA, it helps stabilize the grid. Yie also serves as a link for power trade with the Democratic Republic of the Congo and Angola. It is operated by the Société Nationale d'Électricité (SNE).",
